# =============================================================================
# The Cadenza repository. The tracked source of truth is the specification tree, the neutral
# build-loop commands (commands/), the entry point (start.sh), the seed toolchain under
# implementation/seed/, the design docs under implementation/design/, and the issue archive
# under issues/. Locally, `trunk` is the integration branch (mapped onto origin/main via PR);
# the hub is a bare repo, so all work happens in worktrees under the gitignored .claude/.
# Ignored below: the built `implementation/stable` binary, the target/ dirs, and the gitignored
# .claude/ (the local install target for commands/ + skills/, plus the fleet state in
# .claude/fleet/ — registry, inboxes, per-agent worktrees, and the live work queue that the
# pr-sync agent mirrors into the tracked issues/ archive).
# =============================================================================

# Editor / OS / agent-local
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
.direnv/
result
result-*
.claude/

# stray editor/rust-analyzer flycheck output at repo root
target/

# Compiled seed compiler binary (regenerable via cargo build)
implementation/stable
Cargo.lock
# ...but TRACK the ROOT workspace lock (operator 2026-08-03: "commit the Cargo.lock, otherwise we don't
# get determinism"). Anchored `/Cargo.lock` un-ignores ONLY the repo-root lock — nested crate locks stay
# ignored except where a crate adds its own scoped negation (cdz-runtime/cdz-nfc/the guest fixtures do).
# The nix seed-compiler build (buildRustPackage) + `--locked` CI both need this tracked to vendor/pin.
!/Cargo.lock

# The tracked `fleet/` source dir (role bodies, window.sh, contract) also gets used as an agent scratch
# area — `fleet/scratch/` holds work-in-progress .patch/handoff files that are NOT source and must never
# be committed. They leaked onto origin once (two record-eq migration .patch files swept into an unrelated
# commit via `git add`, PR-review 2026-08-15); ignore the whole dir so scratch artifacts can't be tracked.
fleet/scratch/

# `cdz run-ml` / `cdz run-emitted` write a pid-stamped driver into the compiler-ml src dir (imports
# resolve entry-dir-relative, so it MUST live beside the sources — not a temp dir). They clean up on a
# normal exit, but a SIGKILL'd run (gate-batch contention, or a killed test) can leave one behind; ignore
# the whole `zz-run-…-driver-` prefix so a stray driver never pollutes git status or a `git add -A`.
implementation/compiler-ml/src/zz-run-ml-driver-*.cdz
implementation/compiler-ml/src/zz-run-emitted-driver-*.cdz

# `cargo xtask wasm-opt-gaps` / `nix run .#wasm-opt-gaps` writes this whole-corpus optimality-gap dump
# (~1.4MB, thousands of gap records). Operator: do NOT commit it (too massive) — it is a regenerable,
# advisory artifact; the VALUE is the analysis/report (near-optimal %, outliers) v-wasm-opt delivers from
# it, not the raw dump. Ignore the generated path so a future run's output can't be accidentally committed.
implementation/design/wasm-opt-gaps.sexp

# cdz-platform contract schemas are now BUILD-TIME-generated (v-xtask-decompose xtask-codegen-contracts
# #5209 → the cdzPlatformContracts nix derivation → overlay-staged into cdz-platform's compile sites),
# per the operator codegen→build-time-nix directive. NOT committed — regenerable/advisory; the nix build
# emits them. Ignore so a local `xtask codegen`/stray run can't re-commit them.
/implementation/seed/crates/cdz-platform/src/contracts/

# fleet prune-cron liveness heartbeats (runtime artifact, never tracked)
fleet/*.last-run
